{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2917459","formula":"Ca₂Mn₃P₃H₆O₁₇","hill":"Ca2H6Mn3O17P3","elements":["H","O","P","Ca","Mn"],"composition":{"H":6.0,"O":17.0,"P":3.0,"Ca":2.0,"Mn":3.0},"names":{"en":"Robertsite"},"descriptions":{"en":"Robertsite, Ca3(Mn3+)4[(OH)3| (PO4)2]2·3(H2O) (alternatively formulated Ca2(Mn3(PO4)3O2)(H2O)3), is a secondary phosphate mineral named for Willard Lincoln Roberts (1923–1987), mineralogist and professor at South Dakota School of Mines in Rapid City, South Dakota. The type locality for Robertsite is the Tip Top mine, Custer County, South Dakota, US. Robertsite occurs at the Tip Top Mine as minute crystal aggregates and crusts found on quartz associated with triphylite. It is a dark reddish brown to black monoclinic mineral."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-1182836","atoms":138,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[8.869,0.0,0.0],[0.0,13.478,0.0],[-2.357,0.0,11.058]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":2.854,"y":1.717,"z":0.746,"el":"Ca"},{"x":4.837,"y":8.456,"z":4.783,"el":"Ca"},{"x":3.659,"y":11.761,"z":10.312,"el":"Ca"},{"x":1.675,"y":5.022,"z":6.275,"el":"Ca"},{"x":3.877,"y":5.106,"z":9.478,"el":"Ca"},{"x":1.458,"y":11.845,"z":7.109,"el":"Ca"},{"x":2.636,"y":8.372,"z":1.58,"el":"Ca"},{"x":5.055,"y":1.633,"z":3.949,"el":"Ca"},{"x":-1.178,"y":6.739,"z":5.529,"el":"Mn"},{"x":7.691,"y":6.739,"z":5.529,"el":"Mn"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Mn"},{"x":-2.357,"y":0.0,"z":11.058,"el":"Mn"},{"x":0.0,"y":13.478,"z":0.0,"el":"Mn"},{"x":-2.357,"y":13.478,"z":11.058,"el":"Mn"},{"x":8.869,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Mn"},{"x":6.513,"y":0.0,"z":11.058,"el":"Mn"},{"x":8.869,"y":13.478,"z":0.0,"el":"Mn"},{"x":6.513,"y":13.478,"z":11.058,"el":"Mn"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.739,"z":0.0,"e